+/* glass/engage-stage.css
+   THE ENGAGED STAGE (composables/motion/engage/stage.ts): the ladder's ENGAGED rung.
+   Every engaged control grows where it stands, in flow, under every modality (Q-3′ (i)),
+   so it paints exactly what its place paints; the stage writes the reach the grow may
+   spend inline. The world is not veiled (O-103d (5)). */
+
+/* THE GUTTER CAP, AND THE REACH. Inline, the grow may spend only the clearance the
+   control has beyond the page gutter (`--space-section`, the spacing register's "page
+   gutter" rung, read at the root as `--stage-read-gutter`, utilities/engage.css):
+   1 + 2·max(0, room − gutter)/width, at most the grow. A control already on its gutter (a
+   full-width phone slider) keeps its width and grows along the block axis alone. The
+   stage computes it in the host's own px and writes it as the number it is
+   (stage.ts `writeReach`): a calc here would set script-written px against the gutter's
+   `rem`, which one engine resolves in a different frame under an ancestor's `zoom`. A
+   refused input is written 1, no inline grow, and the stage says so (CK-21). Registered
+   so a host off the stage reads 0, which the held recipe's `--rung-grow` of 0 holds at
+   ×1. */
+@property --stage-reach {
+    syntax: "<number>";
+    inherits: false;
+    initial-value: 0;
+}
